WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:02.380
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: You guys!

00:00:02.380 --> 00:00:04.300
We're here! It's happening!

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:07.860
How are you?

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:10.040
I'm Yvette Nicole Brown, thanks for coming you guys.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.020
We're about to start the most amazing panel at Comic Con,

00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:13.240
I don't care what anybody says.

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:14.680
So let's get started.

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:16.280
Where are all my Oncers?

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:19.820
[crowd cheers]

00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:23.480
Alright, you guys, I wanna just get started and just bring everybody out,

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:26.780
so we're gonna start with the creators of this fabulous show,

00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:30.060
let's bring out Eddie Kitsis and Adam Horowitz.

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:34.200
Hello, handsome fellas.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:39.160
Next, we have the one that is charming and wonderful,

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:41.920
Mr. Josh Dallas.

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:49.760
Making her triumphant return to Comic Con,

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:51.920
give it up for Ginnifer Goodwin!

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:52.840
Snow White!

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.620
Next, we have the rogueishly handsome Captain Hook,

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:00.900
Colin O'Donoghue!

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:10.000
Please keep your applause going for the beautiful and newly dark

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:12.520
Emma Swan, Jennifer Morrison!

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:19.800
We have the vivacious and redeemed Evil Queen,

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:20.760
Lana Parrilla.

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:28.900
We have the man who only takes for the good of others,

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:30.960
our Robin Hood, Sean Maguire.

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:38.740
We have the beautiful one who makes us green with envy because of her talent,

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:41.620
bring out Rebecca Mader, the Wicked Witch!

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:47.520
Please say hello to the winsome and graceful Belle,

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:48.700
Emilie de Ravin.

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:55.900
And last but not least, the man whose heart is now as white as Snow's last name,

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:59.160
Rumplestiltskin himself, Robert Carlyle.

00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:15.580
I, to start, you know, that doggone Author has been a problem for me

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:17.800
Anybody else got a problem with Isaac, the Author?

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:19.400
He's a problem.

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:24.700
So what I need to know is, how much of what we've been seeing and enjoying

00:02:24.820 --> 00:02:30.980
has been his hand, and how much has been free will and fate... help me, Adam and Eddie, help me.

00:02:32.260 --> 00:02:35.700
&gt;&gt;ADAM: Well for the most part, it's been free will.

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:36.820
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Okay.

00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:41.840
&gt;&gt;ADAM: And Isaac, as we saw last season, decided, you know, like any good author,

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:44.340
that he was going to change things for his own betterment.

00:02:44.340 --> 00:02:47.100
And once he did that, things got out of control.

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:52.000
But, he wasn't pushing things and changing the free will of the characters,

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:57.240
the characters have been operating under their own free will, and desires, and falling in love,

00:02:57.240 --> 00:03:00.760
and all that other stuff without, you know, his push.

00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:07.720
And then we saw, hopefully, in the finale last year, how he kind of molded things to his own betterment.

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:10.120
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Okay.  So he's not purely evil.

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:11.840
I don't like him, y'all.  I don't.  Not a fan.

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:12.360
[crowd laughs]

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:13.000
Not a fan.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:14.440
Love the actor, hate the character.  Okay.

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:15.920
&gt;&gt;EDDIE: Never trust a writer.

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:20.000
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: I want to throw this down to Emilie, um

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:25.520
it has been quite a year for Belle, um, she has been profoundly betrayed by her love,

00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:28.040
she found her power by banishing him with the dagger,

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:32.600
she journeyed to Arendelle to try to find information about her mom,

00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:35.660
she found rebound love, um,

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:40.980
it was a rebound y'all, that's not real, that Will thing is not gonna last.

00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:44.600
What do you, Emilie, want for Belle in Season 5?

00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:46.120
&gt;&gt;EMILIE: A vacation.

00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:47.460
[laughter]

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:50.080
Maybe the Bahamas for a few months.

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:56.000
Uh, yeah, no she has, wow, when you list it off, huh.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:56.500
Damn.

00:03:56.600 --> 00:03:57.240
[laughs]

00:03:58.520 --> 00:04:05.960
You know, she's forever, um, forever holding herself together, taking care of this one,

00:04:07.020 --> 00:04:09.500
[crowd cheers]

00:04:09.860 --> 00:04:15.080
and, you know, she's a strong young woman, but there's also a point where she really has to

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:19.000
put her foot down and make probably the biggest decision of her adult life,

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:24.320
um, in regard to, not just her relationship with Rumple but with her relationship with herself

00:04:24.340 --> 00:04:29.140
of where she's gonna head, what's important to her, and, uh, yeah obviously,

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:40.380
as everyone else, been thrown into a massive situation of us all trying to help Miss Swan not

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:44.940
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: There's shenanigans down here on this end of the stage.

00:04:44.940 --> 00:04:46.060
&gt;&gt;EDDIE: Sorry Emilie.

00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:47.500
&gt;&gt;GINNIFER: We're so professional.

00:04:47.500 --> 00:04:49.160
&gt;&gt;EMILIE: We started the name swapping, guys, okay?

00:04:49.160 --> 00:04:51.820
&gt;&gt;LANA: Can you tell that we've been working together for quite some time?

00:04:52.780 --> 00:04:54.740
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: I wanna, you guys, before we go any further,

00:04:54.740 --> 00:04:59.500
last year we had everyone line up for questions early on, so if you guys have a question,

00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:02.700
can you guys find your way to the, uh, the mic now?

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:06.640
Well you don't need to run, I just...safely!  I don't know.

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:10.680
She...I think she should be first.  She's working for it, you guys.  She wants it more than you guys do.

00:05:11.180 --> 00:05:16.920
Okay, um, Robert, when we talked last year, you and I, yes, you and I,

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:20.600
when we talked last year, you said that Rumple was an addict.

00:05:20.600 --> 00:05:25.680
You said that he was addicted to magic and to power, so now we see that he's kinda lost both.

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:30.260
So how do you think that he's going to deal with the loss of the two things that he loves the most,

00:05:30.260 --> 00:05:31.560
or he's addicted to, I should say.

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:37.480
&gt;&gt;ROBERT: Well, that's a difficult question to answer, really, without giving too much away this time around

00:05:37.780 --> 00:05:41.400
but he, uh, the incarnation of Rumple this time around is

00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:44.940
slightly different from what you guys have been used to seeing.

00:05:45.380 --> 00:05:50.780
Um, he has lost his mantle as the Dark One, but that's not to say that

00:05:50.780 --> 00:05:54.600
he still doesn't have that same kind of, um, trickery about him.

00:05:55.060 --> 00:05:56.260
He still has that.

00:05:56.500 --> 00:06:01.240
Um, Adam and Eddie are the ones to ask about how this thing's gonna go,

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:06.460
and as regards to Mr. Gold, he's presently in a coma, so he's not doing too much.

00:06:06.680 --> 00:06:07.540
[laughter]

00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:15.040
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Since we're gonna stay in the "Lost" area, I wanna come down to Miss Lana Parrilla.

00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:17.760
[crowd cheers]

00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:21.220
I'm gonna jump around,  I didn't jump over those two wonderful newbies,

00:06:21.220 --> 00:06:24.220
I'm coming back to them, I just got this question for Lana.

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:25.360
&gt;&gt;FAN: Happy birthday!

00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:27.160
&gt;&gt;LANA: Oh, thanks!

00:06:29.180 --> 00:06:34.180
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Lana, this year we got a further glimpse into what Regina has been through in her life.

00:06:34.180 --> 00:06:39.880
Um, even the Author said that out of all the characters, Regina has been screwed over the most.

00:06:39.880 --> 00:06:40.380
[laughter]

00:06:40.380 --> 00:06:40.880
Yeah.

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:46.240
Um, I was moved by the realization that even your mother, Cora, told you

00:06:46.240 --> 00:06:48.440
"You're not gonna be happy.  You don't know how."

00:06:48.440 --> 00:06:53.480
So how does this affect Regina's-- I know it's horrible! It's her mama!

00:06:53.480 --> 00:06:56.760
&gt;&gt;LANA: I think it made for a very difficult life.

00:06:56.760 --> 00:06:59.900
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Yeah.  How does this affect Regina's way of looking at life

00:06:59.900 --> 00:07:01.080
and what she thinks is possible for her?

00:07:01.760 --> 00:07:07.260
&gt;&gt;LANA: Well I think she deep down, felt, at one point, that she can never truly be happy,

00:07:07.340 --> 00:07:16.040
and, um, and that's why she was so bad and evil, and committed all these horrible acts.

00:07:16.680 --> 00:07:22.560
But, um, it's being surrounded by the heroes, I guess, that have--

00:07:22.560 --> 00:07:28.640
and really Emma and Henry, that have changed this sort of perception.

00:07:29.980 --> 00:07:34.900
But hearing that, for her, growing up, by her mother and her father wishing happiness upon her

00:07:34.900 --> 00:07:40.820
and her going in an opposite direction, um, you know, she's come full circle.

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:46.280
But I think it's having the familial support that has really given her hope.

00:07:46.740 --> 00:07:49.140
And, she found love.

00:07:50.040 --> 00:07:52.960
[crowd cheers]

00:07:54.360 --> 00:07:59.180
I think she's really now starting to embrace it and accept that she can be happy.

00:07:59.520 --> 00:08:02.240
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: I mean, since you threw to him.  I was gonna go to him later but he's right there.

00:08:04.640 --> 00:08:09.540
Um, I want to know... This is a tough one.

00:08:09.920 --> 00:08:13.680
Sean Maguire, who do you think is Robin Hood's true love?

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:18.820
Because I see the connection that he has with Regina, but, you know,

00:08:18.820 --> 00:08:20.780
&gt;&gt;SEAN: Colin, stop looking at me.

00:08:20.780 --> 00:08:24.860
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Listen here, Rebecca.  Rebecca, Rebecca, don't you start, Rebecca.

00:08:24.860 --> 00:08:26.540
Don't you start, Rebecca.

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:30.040
Look.  There's been some trickery...

00:08:30.040 --> 00:08:31.980
&gt;&gt;SEAN: Are you asking me my peronal opinion?

00:08:31.980 --> 00:08:33.060
&gt;&gt;LANA: Answer this very carefully.

00:08:33.060 --> 00:08:36.700
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: I would like you to answer as yourself and the character, please, since you brought it up as an option.

00:08:36.700 --> 00:08:40.600
&gt;&gt;SEAN: I only go by what Adam and Eddie write.

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:42.600
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Good answer.

00:08:42.900 --> 00:08:48.940
&gt;&gt;SEAN: And the way that I've read it is that he's pretty madly in love with this one.

00:08:49.520 --> 00:08:51.160
[crowd cheers]

00:08:51.680 --> 00:08:54.800
I may be wrong, but that's how I interpreted it.

00:08:55.500 --> 00:08:57.180
This one's just a meanie.

00:08:58.340 --> 00:08:59.860
And rather deceitful.

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:04.620
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Yes.  I'm still gonna hold off on Rebecca, I need some time before I get to you, I gotta...

00:09:04.620 --> 00:09:07.880
I gotta get my mind right girl, I gotta get my mind right.

00:09:07.880 --> 00:09:11.380
I'm gonna bump over to something that was very delightful for me this year.

00:09:11.380 --> 00:09:16.520
Um, I loved everything you guys did.  I love the show, I'm a Oncer, but my favorite scenes this season

00:09:16.520 --> 00:09:20.060
have invariably involved Ginnifer and Josh being horrible.

00:09:20.060 --> 00:09:21.940
[laughter]

00:09:21.940 --> 00:09:26.740
Snowing's descent into criminal mastermindom has been just my favorite thing.

00:09:26.740 --> 00:09:30.660
I wanted to know, how much fun was it to portray the darker sides of

00:09:30.660 --> 00:09:32.020
Snow and Prince Charming?

00:09:32.020 --> 00:09:33.560
Y'all were wretched.  Wretched at times!

00:09:33.560 --> 00:09:36.140
&gt;&gt;GINNIFER: I could do that all day, every day.

00:09:36.140 --> 00:09:38.620
&gt;&gt;JOSH: Every day? Like in real life?

00:09:38.620 --> 00:09:39.660
&gt;&gt;GINNIFER: Even at home.

00:09:39.660 --> 00:09:46.420
Um, I would like to give an answer full of artistic integrity, but the truth is, I mostly break out into giggles, because it's so much fun.

00:09:46.420 --> 00:09:49.640
&gt;&gt;JENNIFER: The cameraman's confused because we messed up the names.

00:09:49.720 --> 00:09:52.260
[laughter]

00:09:52.260 --> 00:09:54.200
Sorry.  Sorry buddy!

00:09:55.080 --> 00:09:56.360
&gt;&gt;EDDIE: Finally.

00:09:56.880 --> 00:09:58.240
&gt;&gt;JOSH: Find us now.

00:09:58.240 --> 00:10:00.180
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: What was that, "Adam"?

00:10:00.180 --> 00:10:01.540
&gt;&gt;JOSH: Find us now.

00:10:01.540 --> 00:10:02.440
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: He's got Adam.

00:10:02.800 --> 00:10:04.500
&gt;&gt;LANA: Josh, your name's Adam.

00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:05.800
&gt;&gt;JENNIFER: You'll just be Jennifer Morrison.

00:10:06.380 --> 00:10:07.340
&gt;&gt;JOSH: What?

00:10:07.340 --> 00:10:09.880
&gt;&gt;LANA: You have Adam Horowitz instead of you.

00:10:10.860 --> 00:10:16.760
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Adam, how was it for Josh to be evil?

00:10:17.020 --> 00:10:18.380
&gt;&gt;ADAM: It was good.

00:10:22.940 --> 00:10:26.240
&gt;&gt;JOSH: Yeah, it was great to be able to explore a different side of him, for sure.

00:10:26.240 --> 00:10:33.180
And if we get the opportunity to go back there, it would be great fun.

00:10:33.180 --> 00:10:34.180
&gt;&gt;GINNIFER: Yes please.

00:10:34.180 --> 00:10:34.680
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Yes.

00:10:34.680 --> 00:10:39.540
&gt;&gt;JENNIFER: I think Josh really liked the guyliner.  I think he was happy to have the guyliner.

00:10:41.480 --> 00:10:42.320
&gt;&gt;GINNIFER: The guylliner.

00:10:42.320 --> 00:10:48.480
&gt;&gt;JOSH: Guyliner.  Guyliner is, hey, I was against the guyliner for a long time, but now I kinda like it.

00:10:48.480 --> 00:10:49.720
&gt;&gt;GINNIFER: Even at home?

00:10:49.720 --> 00:10:53.280
&gt;&gt;ADAM: We doubled down on the guyliner.  We said, "Josh, more guyliner for you." And he loved it.

00:10:53.280 --> 00:10:54.360
&gt;&gt;GINNIFER: More manscara.

00:10:55.560 --> 00:10:57.000
&gt;&gt;COLIN: Whoa.  Whoa.

00:10:57.000 --> 00:10:58.460
&gt;&gt;ADAM: No one's gonna take yours away, Colin.

00:10:58.460 --> 00:10:59.660
&gt;&gt;JOSH: I said I like it, I like it.

00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:04.560
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: This question is for Jennifer, our Emma Swan.

00:11:04.940 --> 00:11:08.460
No claps? I'm gonna clap for her.  She's gonna go dark.

00:11:08.460 --> 00:11:09.500
[crowd cheers]

00:11:09.500 --> 00:11:12.900
Let me say that name and y'all don't give her what she's due?

00:11:12.900 --> 00:11:18.720
Okay, Jennifer, Emma finds out this season, last season, that being good and the Savior

00:11:18.720 --> 00:11:23.880
was not exactly born in her, that there was some trickery by these two that caused it to be so strong.

00:11:23.880 --> 00:11:29.200
Has that affected her confidence in being the Savior and what she means to the residents of Storybrooke?

00:11:29.200 --> 00:11:34.300
&gt;&gt;JENNIFER: Uh, yeah.  I mean, I think a lot of Season 4 was about her confidence really being shaken

00:11:34.300 --> 00:11:41.740
because when you believe that you've overcome obstacles on your own, you believe that you've found

00:11:41.740 --> 00:11:47.400
that strength within yourself.  And so, not only did it feel like a betrayal to think that her parents,

00:11:47.400 --> 00:11:54.160
who she built up to be these really idealist, good images, had, you know, hurt her,

00:11:54.160 --> 00:12:01.580
um, she felt like this was not necessarily her own accomplishment to have stayed good

00:12:01.580 --> 00:12:07.060
despite all of the things that had happened in her life.  And so, um, that definitely undercut her confidence

00:12:07.060 --> 00:12:11.600
in her belief in her strength and in herself.

00:12:11.600 --> 00:12:15.400
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: I, um, something just came to mind as we were talking about this.

00:12:15.400 --> 00:12:19.180
Storybrooke is not exactly safe.  I don't know if anybody's aware of that.

00:12:19.180 --> 00:12:21.460
It's not safe, stuff happens all the time.

00:12:21.460 --> 00:12:24.260
&gt;&gt;JOSH: Really bad sheriffs, really bad sheriffs.

00:12:24.260 --> 00:12:31.260
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Some bad stuff went down last year, there was ice walls, and the churnabog, and stuff happened, and Cruella, a lot of stuff.

00:12:31.260 --> 00:12:35.120
And at times people can leave.  Not always, but sometimes they can leave.

00:12:35.120 --> 00:12:36.860
And I'm trying to figure out why people stay.

00:12:39.320 --> 00:12:40.960
&gt;&gt;ADAM: That's an excellent question.

00:12:40.960 --> 00:12:42.100
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Why do they stay, Adam and Eddie?

00:12:42.100 --> 00:12:44.520
&gt;&gt;EDDIE: That is a great question, and  think we have a video--

00:12:44.520 --> 00:12:45.180
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Is there a video?

00:12:45.180 --> 00:12:45.680
&gt;&gt;ADAM: Yeah.

00:12:45.680 --> 00:12:49.780
&gt;&gt;EDDIE: I think we should ask some Storybrooke residents why they stay.

00:12:49.780 --> 00:12:56.180
The people that you don't see.  For all the heroes, they're the people that are cobblers, and have real jobs.

00:12:56.180 --> 00:12:58.640
&gt;&gt;ADAM: There's many, many people who are suffering in Storybrooke.

00:12:58.640 --> 00:12:59.900
&gt;&gt;EDDIE: Yeah.  Let's see what that is.

00:12:59.900 --> 00:13:04.220
&gt;&gt;ADAM: We have the writers of "Once Upon A Time," are here, we don't do this by ourselves.

00:13:04.220 --> 00:13:05.440
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Stand up, you guys, where are you?

00:13:05.440 --> 00:13:08.280
&gt;&gt;EDDIE: Stand up, writers!  Let's see where you are!

00:13:08.280 --> 00:13:09.320
[crowd cheers]

00:13:09.320 --> 00:13:10.160
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Oh, hey guys!

00:13:10.200 --> 00:13:11.880
&gt;&gt;EDDIE: There they are!

00:13:11.880 --> 00:13:14.200
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Thank you for all you do.

00:13:15.340 --> 00:13:22.060
&gt;&gt;EDDIE: We are up here but we could not do it without those people right there, so please harass them after.

00:13:22.060 --> 00:13:22.560
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Yes.

00:13:22.560 --> 00:13:24.300
&gt;&gt;EDDIE: Let them know how lovely they are.

00:13:25.260 --> 00:13:27.320
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Um, this question is for Colin.

00:13:27.720 --> 00:13:30.080
[crowd cheers]

00:13:30.800 --> 00:13:38.340
Hey, Colin.  Um, for all of Hook's previous scoundrel-like tendencies, he's proven this year to be an upstanding guy.

00:13:38.340 --> 00:13:41.960
So what do you think has been his greatest challenge to achieving complete redemption?

00:13:41.960 --> 00:13:44.420
Is it his temper? Cause that flared up this year.

00:13:44.420 --> 00:13:47.940
Is it pride? That came up this year.

00:13:47.940 --> 00:13:50.240
His fear came up this year.

00:13:50.240 --> 00:13:51.680
What is it?

00:13:51.680 --> 00:13:54.780
&gt;&gt;COLIN: Can I just say you look wonderful today, Yvette.

00:13:54.780 --> 00:13:56.180
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Why, yes, you can.

00:13:58.060 --> 00:14:10.720
&gt;&gt;COLIN: I think, you know, Hook has sort of been battling darkness for hundreds of years, and he found love with Emma.

00:14:14.580 --> 00:14:21.540
So, I think, you know, he's desperately been trying to hold on to that, trying to be a better man,

00:14:21.540 --> 00:14:27.700
to keep her heart sort of safe, much like, you know, Charming and Snow, he wants to protect her.

00:14:27.700 --> 00:14:35.120
But he has been a villain.  And his girlfriend's nasty now, so,

00:14:37.460 --> 00:14:38.400
I mean in a good way.

00:14:38.400 --> 00:14:39.780
&gt;&gt;JENNIFER: Oh yeah.  Okay.

00:14:40.460 --> 00:14:48.400
&gt;&gt;COLIN: So, who knows what's gonna happen.  But I think he really struggled with trying to stay on the right path last season.

00:14:49.080 --> 00:14:52.360
And it'll be interesting to see where he goes now.

00:14:52.360 --> 00:14:56.840
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Okay.  I, um, you guys, there's something happening at Comic Con that's been selling out.

00:14:56.840 --> 00:14:59.740
Are you guys aware of these Funko Pop?

00:14:59.740 --> 00:15:00.780
[crowd cheers]

00:15:00.780 --> 00:15:04.180
Cause, um, there's one of Regina

00:15:04.180 --> 00:15:06.840
[crowd cheers]

00:15:06.840 --> 00:15:11.800
I know this is not about me, but I feel like, for being here, somebody should've gave me one

00:15:13.020 --> 00:15:14.460
&gt;&gt;EDDIE: They didn't give me one.

00:15:14.780 --> 00:15:17.180
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Why I gotta beg for stuff up here?

00:15:17.180 --> 00:15:19.280
&gt;&gt;LANA: I think we could make that happen...

00:15:19.660 --> 00:15:23.760
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: What?  What now?  Say what?  What's happening?

00:15:23.760 --> 00:15:24.260
&gt;&gt;LANA: Ta-da

00:15:24.260 --> 00:15:25.460
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: What?!

00:15:25.640 --> 00:15:26.680
[crowd cheers]

00:15:29.420 --> 00:15:30.540
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Thank you, pumpkin.

00:15:30.920 --> 00:15:37.400
&gt;&gt;EDDIE: Hey, there will be a set of six "Once Upon A Time" Funko Pop dolls available

00:15:37.400 --> 00:15:45.280
online and in stores early October, so Oncers, lets show Funko how strong we are.

00:15:45.280 --> 00:15:47.660
Let's buy these and have them sell out.

00:15:48.060 --> 00:15:48.560
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Yes.

00:15:48.560 --> 00:15:50.960
&gt;&gt;GINNIFER: I can tell you they're actually already available for preorder online

00:15:50.960 --> 00:15:53.120
because our son already has a set coming.

00:15:55.360 --> 00:15:57.560
&gt;&gt;ADAM: There was supposed to be one of me.

00:16:00.560 --> 00:16:01.580
Nah.  No there wasn't.

00:16:02.380 --> 00:16:06.780
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Before we go to the audience questions, which will be next, I gotta go down to Rebecca.

00:16:07.600 --> 00:16:08.220
Hi, Rebecca.

00:16:08.220 --> 00:16:09.400
&gt;&gt;REBECCA: Hello, gorgeous.

00:16:09.400 --> 00:16:14.280
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: You scare me a little bit.  I'm a little scared of you. I mean, don't look at me like that!

00:16:14.280 --> 00:16:15.380
&gt;&gt;REBECCA: You should be scared.

00:16:15.380 --> 00:16:16.280
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: I should be scared!

00:16:16.980 --> 00:16:21.240
Okay this is serious.  Look, I think you're great and I think you're an amazing actress,

00:16:21.240 --> 00:16:23.500
&gt;&gt;REBECCA: But.  There's a but coming, isn't there?

00:16:23.500 --> 00:16:24.560
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: But you scare me a little bit.

00:16:24.560 --> 00:16:27.140
This is what I wanna know.  This is why you scare me, cause you're brilliant.

00:16:27.680 --> 00:16:34.880
Zelena has been a bratty child, and on a dime, she has shifted to being the most evil, scary, wicked thing you've ever seen.

00:16:34.900 --> 00:16:41.620
I'm an actor.  I'm a hack, I'm not that great, I'm not as great as her.  But I know, as an actor, it is very difficult to make that turn.

00:16:41.620 --> 00:16:45.800
So I wanna know, what has that been like for you, as an actor, as a thespian, on "Once Upon A Time"?

00:16:45.800 --> 00:16:50.640
&gt;&gt;REBECCA: It's been wicked!  It's so much fun!  This is the best character I've ever played in my life.

00:16:50.640 --> 00:16:55.600
I love playing someone just so batshit crazy.  It's so much fun.

00:16:55.600 --> 00:17:00.000
Zelena is a complete psychopath.  This is the best thing that's ever happened to me.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:07.480
I think the reason it's so easy to play someone so awful is because she thinks she's delightful.

00:17:09.100 --> 00:17:13.320
I mean, she is totally incognizant of the reality of who she really is.

00:17:13.320 --> 00:17:17.700
And she is on a mission, she believes she's her own hero, so I just trust in that.

00:17:17.700 --> 00:17:23.800
Rather than trying to play awful, I trust in the fact that she needs to vindicate herself and find her own happy ending

00:17:23.800 --> 00:17:28.440
because she feels incredibly wronged, and she is on a mission to get what she truly deserved

00:17:28.440 --> 00:17:29.940
cause she believes she's right.

00:17:29.940 --> 00:17:34.180
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Tell me this, I notice things, you guys, I'm a nerd, I watch, really, for the minutia.

00:17:34.180 --> 00:17:38.540
Zelena's been looking at us directly in the camera.  Has she not?  She looked at us in the hospital,

00:17:38.540 --> 00:17:41.500
and she looked at us in that mirror.  You guys notice she looked right at us?

00:17:41.500 --> 00:17:42.180
&gt;&gt;REBECCA: Did I?

00:17:42.180 --> 00:17:43.040
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: I'm not crazy!

00:17:43.100 --> 00:17:46.500
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: She looked, there are two-- Go back and get your DVRs going.

00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:49.240
There are two moments when Zelena looks into your soul.

00:17:49.260 --> 00:17:55.780
I'm not kidding. She did it in New York twice, when she's in the hospital with Rumple she looks right down the barrel,

00:17:55.780 --> 00:18:03.340
And there's a moment when she's hugging Robin Hood and she looks in the mirror and she looks into your soul.

00:18:03.340 --> 00:18:04.760
&gt;&gt;REBECCA: Oh yeah!  Thank you!

00:18:04.760 --> 00:18:06.820
&gt;&gt;SEAN: I felt like she was looking right at me too!

00:18:06.820 --> 00:18:08.020
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: I know I didn't miss this.

00:18:08.020 --> 00:18:11.860
Alright, this is my stuff, I gotta get-- this is my time with him too!

00:18:12.440 --> 00:18:14.680
Okay.  You did that, I know you did.

00:18:14.680 --> 00:18:18.820
&gt;&gt;REBECCA: No, no, that was a really fun day at work, when Sean had to kiss everybody in the room.

00:18:18.820 --> 00:18:23.440
And there was this moment where we like, switched, and so Maid Marian and me were all kissing him,

00:18:23.440 --> 00:18:28.300
and there was a mirror right there, and I was like, "Ooh, that would be really sick and twisted if I just like opened my eyes and looked in the mirror.

00:18:28.300 --> 00:18:29.380
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: And she did!  I'm telling you, she did it.

00:18:29.380 --> 00:18:30.760
&gt;&gt;REBECCA: It made it really, really twisted.

00:18:30.760 --> 00:18:33.200
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: She looked right at us.  Okay, let go to an audience question.

00:18:34.100 --> 00:18:36.500
Are you there? Hi, honey!

00:18:37.440 --> 00:18:38.640
&gt;&gt;KATIE: Hi, I'm Katie.

00:18:38.640 --> 00:18:39.260
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Hi, Katie.

00:18:39.260 --> 00:18:46.260
&gt;&gt;KATIE: My question is for Colin. If the Author was real and you could have him change one thing about your life,

00:18:46.260 --> 00:18:47.380
what would it be?

00:18:47.780 --> 00:18:50.020
&gt;&gt;COLIN: About my life, as Colin?

00:18:51.260 --> 00:18:53.800
About my life?  Wow.

00:18:55.380 --> 00:18:57.440
&gt;&gt;JENNIFER: That's deep.  Good luck with that.

00:18:57.880 --> 00:18:59.380
&gt;&gt;COLIN: Let me answer that as Captain Hook.

00:19:00.420 --> 00:19:06.340
I think I would like to have two hands.  I think that would be probably the thing I would say.

00:19:07.320 --> 00:19:13.080
Dear Mr. Author, please could I have two hands so I can feel something with my left hand.

00:19:13.760 --> 00:19:14.400
Hey.  Hey!

00:19:15.380 --> 00:19:16.500
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Heyo!

00:19:16.500 --> 00:19:17.700
&gt;&gt;COLIN: Stop it!

00:19:18.080 --> 00:19:22.520
I genuinely actually didn't mean to make a joke there.  I'm just incredibly funny.

00:19:26.480 --> 00:19:32.380
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Wow.  Y'all don't even know.  Okay can we do another?  Let's do another.

00:19:33.200 --> 00:19:37.280
&gt;&gt;MARISSA: Hi, this question's for-- Oh, my name's Marissa.

00:19:37.280 --> 00:19:38.080
&gt;&gt;PANEL: Hi, Marissa.

00:19:38.080 --> 00:19:43.760
&gt;&gt;MARISSA: And this question's for Jennifer.  So since Colin, you have to fake an accent in your show,

00:19:43.760 --> 00:19:46.720
I wanted Jennifer to try and do the Irish accent.

00:19:47.020 --> 00:19:48.220
&gt;&gt;COLIN: Yeah!!!

00:19:48.220 --> 00:19:49.260
[crowd cheers]

00:19:49.260 --> 00:19:50.620
&gt;&gt;SEAN: Well done.

00:19:50.620 --> 00:19:51.560
&gt;&gt;ADAM: I think we all would.

00:19:51.560 --> 00:19:52.860
&gt;&gt;SEAN: Well done.

00:19:52.860 --> 00:19:53.820
&gt;&gt;LANA: Oh no.

00:19:53.820 --> 00:19:57.300
&gt;&gt;COLIN: Starting with easy questions.  Let's be having you.

00:19:57.300 --> 00:19:58.720
&gt;&gt;JENNIFER: Let's be having you.

00:19:59.380 --> 00:20:00.740
&gt;&gt;SEAN: Irish Swan.

00:20:00.740 --> 00:20:02.040
&gt;&gt;JENNIFER: Let's be having you.

00:20:02.040 --> 00:20:05.060
&gt;&gt;COLIN: Say "Conas atá tú."

00:20:05.060 --> 00:20:07.020
&gt;&gt;JENNIFER: What? What was-- Is that English?

00:20:07.020 --> 00:20:08.540
&gt;&gt;COLIN: Conas atá tu.

00:20:08.540 --> 00:20:09.660
&gt;&gt;JENNIFER: Conas atá tee.

00:20:09.740 --> 00:20:11.260
&gt;&gt;COLIN: Yeah. Conas atá tú.

00:20:11.340 --> 00:20:13.100
&gt;&gt;JENNIFER: Say it again?

00:20:13.720 --> 00:20:15.240
&gt;&gt;COLIN: Conas atá tú.

00:20:15.240 --> 00:20:17.000
&gt;&gt;JENNIFER: Conas atá tú?

00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:17.960
&gt;&gt;SEAN: Yeah!

00:20:17.960 --> 00:20:19.080
&gt;&gt;COLIN: That's Irish for "How are you?"

00:20:19.080 --> 00:20:22.840
&gt;&gt;JENNIFER: Oh! Conas atá tú.  Conas atá tú.  Conas atá tú.

00:20:23.360 --> 00:20:24.240
Conas atá tú.

00:20:24.240 --> 00:20:25.520
&gt;&gt;ADAM: And scene.

00:20:27.800 --> 00:20:29.900
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Let's do one more, since we have the light.  Go ahead, honey.

00:20:29.900 --> 00:20:36.900
&gt;&gt;JAIMARY: Hi, my name is Jaimary.  My question is for Jennifer, and I wanted to know what your reaction

00:20:36.900 --> 00:20:39.360
to the Season 4 finale was.

00:20:40.480 --> 00:20:48.760
&gt;&gt;JENNIFER: Yeah, I um, I'm really excited.  As an actor, to be able to start Season 5 of a show doing something

00:20:48.760 --> 00:20:56.320
brand new is so exciting.  And I've really, I've been so enjoying playing Emma and

00:20:56.320 --> 00:21:03.940
everything that's come along with it.  But, um, now I get to sorta try something totally new and different

00:21:03.940 --> 00:21:10.200
and, um get to have the fun that these guys have been having.  You know, there is some fun to the villainy.

00:21:10.200 --> 00:21:17.200
Um, and I've spent the whole hiatus kind of digging up my thoughts about it and figuring out what I want to do with it

00:21:17.200 --> 00:21:24.880
and uh, yeah.  I'm just really excited.  I think it's a really great thing.  And I think that also, you know,

00:21:24.880 --> 00:21:31.880
Emma went through a lot in her life, and she had a tough childhood, and she's had to overcome a lot of things,

00:21:31.880 --> 00:21:38.220
and she's always tried to be the bigger person, and she's tried to be the good person, and now that she's

00:21:38.220 --> 00:21:46.220
tethered to the Darkness, she's sort of free of that and, um, I think that in that space, she's gonna face some of

00:21:46.220 --> 00:21:51.540
the Darkness in herself and figure out what that means, and figure out how to truly overcome it instead of

00:21:51.540 --> 00:21:55.800
just repress it.  So, um, I'm excited to see where this journey takes her.

00:21:55.800 --> 00:22:02.880
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: I think this is a great time to segue into the dark elephant in the room,

00:22:02.880 --> 00:22:06.800
the swaniness of it all, the Dark Swaniness of it.

00:22:07.660 --> 00:22:09.740
You guys.  It's happening.

00:22:09.740 --> 00:22:12.760
&gt;&gt;ADAM: Would you guys like to take a look at Emma as the Dark Swan?

00:22:12.760 --> 00:22:13.800
[crowd cheers]

00:22:13.800 --> 00:22:15.460
&gt;&gt;EDDIE: Who wants to see the Dark Swan?

00:22:16.260 --> 00:22:17.060
Let's do it.

00:22:17.060 --> 00:22:18.040
&gt;&gt;ADAM: Should we show you?

00:22:18.340 --> 00:22:19.380
[crowd cheers]

00:22:20.320 --> 00:22:20.820
Okay.

00:22:22.240 --> 00:22:23.600
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Alright.

00:22:23.600 --> 00:22:25.340
&gt;&gt;EDDIE: All you had to do was ask.

00:22:26.620 --> 00:22:32.240
&gt;&gt;EDDIE: Everyone up in Vancouver, Steve, and our crew up there,  we couldn't do it without you.

00:22:32.900 --> 00:22:34.020
&gt;&gt;JENNIFER: Amen.

00:22:34.180 --> 00:22:36.120
[applause]

00:22:36.120 --> 00:22:40.280
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: You know what, I'm gonna be honest, I'm not okay.  I''m not okay.

00:22:40.820 --> 00:22:47.140
I had to resist every black person urge I have cause not all of us, but some of us talk back to the screen.

00:22:47.140 --> 00:22:48.500
[laughter]

00:22:48.500 --> 00:22:55.500
Not all of us.  This one does.  And I wanted to tell him not to go in there.  I wanted to save my brother, don't go in-- Okay.  I'm done.

00:22:55.500 --> 00:22:57.360
[laughter]

00:22:57.360 --> 00:23:00.260
I'm very disturbed, and Jennifer, now I'm afraid of you.  Okay.

00:23:01.020 --> 00:23:05.980
I wanna ask this question of the lovely Jennifer, who scared the crap out of me a second ago.

00:23:07.740 --> 00:23:13.800
In my opinion, I felt that Emma sacrificed herself for Regina.  I felt this entire season was a great

00:23:14.140 --> 00:23:18.440
pairing of you two in various ways, I felt like a friendship was truly formed.

00:23:18.440 --> 00:23:22.860
A love was truly formed.  You guys actually care about each other and I felt like in that moment,

00:23:22.860 --> 00:23:30.140
you gave up everything for Regina.  But you have some other thoughts about it as well in that moment

00:23:30.140 --> 00:23:31.260
when she became Dark Swan.

00:23:31.260 --> 00:23:37.120
&gt;&gt;JENNIFER: I mean, I think that if Regina were the only person in danger she would still have made the same choice.

00:23:37.120 --> 00:23:43.660
But from a storytelling perspective, I think it's also important for people to know that the Darkness was threatening the entire town.

00:23:43.660 --> 00:23:44.160
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Right.

00:23:44.200 --> 00:23:49.960
&gt;&gt;JENNIFER: Um, so, although with the friendship that they have formed at this point,

00:23:49.960 --> 00:23:55.000
and as much as she's seen Regina go through, she would absolutely have made that choice either way.

00:23:55.000 --> 00:24:00.400
You know, she had to make a split-second decision, knowing that if that Darkness wasn't tethered to one being

00:24:00.400 --> 00:24:02.260
that it was going to consume everyone in town.

00:24:02.260 --> 00:24:02.760
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Right.

00:24:02.760 --> 00:24:07.080
&gt;&gt;JENNIFER: And everyone would have been lost to it.  So it is sort of twofold.

00:24:07.080 --> 00:24:10.820
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Twofold.  Okay, I wanna go back to Eddie and Adam.  Hi guys.

00:24:10.820 --> 00:24:11.480
&gt;&gt;EDDIE: Hello.

00:24:11.480 --> 00:24:13.940
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Have I told you I love you lately?  I love you both.

00:24:13.940 --> 00:24:15.300
&gt;&gt;EDDIE: Thank you.

00:24:15.300 --> 00:24:19.200
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: I do.  Has the hundredth episode been planned yet, and if so, what do you have in store?

00:24:19.200 --> 00:24:23.240
I didn't say I loved you to get scoop, I just feel like we deserve some scoop.

00:24:23.240 --> 00:24:29.080
&gt;&gt;ADAM: Well, I mean, all we can really say right now is we want to make it very special,

00:24:29.080 --> 00:24:32.620
and we're planning to have the hundredth episode be our spring premiere,

00:24:32.620 --> 00:24:38.740
so, um, you know, we're hard at work at not telling you anything right now.

00:24:39.720 --> 00:24:46.100
&gt;&gt;EDDIE: But we're very proud that we are entering our fifth season and that we are approaching our hundredth episode.

00:24:46.620 --> 00:24:52.800
And for a show that everyone predicted to be cancelled first, I think it is a testament to you, Oncers,

00:24:52.800 --> 00:24:53.300
&gt;&gt;ADAM: Thank you all.

00:24:53.300 --> 00:24:55.060
&gt;&gt;EDDIE: So give yourselves a round of applause.

00:24:56.660 --> 00:24:57.300
We did it.

00:24:57.300 --> 00:25:02.160
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Yes.  Let's bounce to another audience question.  Hi, honey.  Hi!

00:25:02.160 --> 00:25:06.360
&gt;&gt;GRACE: Um, I'm Grace.  My question is for Eddie and Adam.

00:25:06.360 --> 00:25:12.200
As someone who's made lifelong friends through the fandom, what do you think it is about

00:25:12.200 --> 00:25:17.720
this show in particular that makes these strangers into a family?

00:25:18.900 --> 00:25:24.580
&gt;&gt;ADAM: Oh, that's really wonderful to hear.  You know, I don't know, it's like it is magic

00:25:24.580 --> 00:25:29.220
to see you guys and to see this fandom, it just blows our mind every time.

00:25:29.220 --> 00:25:33.260
&gt;&gt;EDDIE: I think that this is a show for believers and people who want to believe,

00:25:33.260 --> 00:25:39.700
and I think that it united a lot of people who are tired of cynicism and believe in magic.

00:25:40.380 --> 00:25:45.820
And I hope it did bring you all together, and I hope you gained lifelong friends because I think

00:25:45.820 --> 00:25:50.880
the reason that we created this show is to add a little hope to the world in any way we could.

00:25:52.620 --> 00:25:53.660
[crowd cheers]

00:25:55.200 --> 00:25:57.800
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Uh, this question is for Ginnifer Goodwin.

00:25:58.540 --> 00:25:59.580
[crowd cheers]

00:25:59.800 --> 00:26:01.160
Yes, she's amazing.

00:26:01.300 --> 00:26:02.900
&gt;&gt;FAN: I love your hair!

00:26:02.900 --> 00:26:03.480
&gt;&gt;GINNIFER: Thank you.

00:26:03.480 --> 00:26:04.820
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: We all love her hair.

00:26:04.820 --> 00:26:05.780
&gt;&gt;GINNIFER: It's hiding the gray.

00:26:05.780 --> 00:26:10.080
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Okay, this is not a question so much a a kudos.  When you had to channel Regina,

00:26:10.080 --> 00:26:13.760
and you know that scene, you guys, where she's speaking?  Right?

00:26:13.760 --> 00:26:18.620
That is some of the most amazing lip-syncing I have ever heard, and I believe there's some information

00:26:18.620 --> 00:26:20.560
you wanna tell us about how that scene came together.

00:26:20.560 --> 00:26:22.620
&gt;&gt;GINNIFER: It was, I mean, it's a bit of a trick.

00:26:22.840 --> 00:26:28.700
Um, Lana actually gave me a recording of how she was going to perform it later,

00:26:28.700 --> 00:26:37.160
so I imitated her on camera by listening to something on my phone, and then she went back

00:26:37.160 --> 00:26:47.620
and did what we call ADR, which is the voiceover done after the fact and she lipsynced her own voice back to my lips.

00:26:48.040 --> 00:26:53.640
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: And I have a tip.  When I did my little small cameo, which I loved, as Ursula,

00:26:53.640 --> 00:26:58.600
Lana had already been Ursula, she had already done her scenes.  And so I ran into her randomly

00:26:58.600 --> 00:27:03.520
at a party, and I said "Hey, how did you do it?" and then I mimicked her as my voice of Ursula.

00:27:03.520 --> 00:27:05.200
So we all just wanna be Lana Parrilla.

00:27:05.780 --> 00:27:07.300
[cheers and laughter]

00:27:09.140 --> 00:27:11.080
This is a question for Robert.  Hi, Robert.

00:27:11.500 --> 00:27:12.100
&gt;&gt;ROBERT: Hi.

00:27:13.000 --> 00:27:20.000
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: You recently directed "The Legend of Barney Thomson."  It was your feature film debut.  Your directorial debut.

00:27:20.000 --> 00:27:21.000
[applause]

00:27:21.000 --> 00:27:25.320
Is there any chance you'd direct an episode of "Once Upon A Time"?

00:27:27.140 --> 00:27:31.880
&gt;&gt;ROBERT: Well, I guess that's a question for Adam and Eddie but they have to see the film yet.  So I don't know.

00:27:31.880 --> 00:27:34.080
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: It's been getting great reviews, don't even try it.

00:27:34.580 --> 00:27:41.300
I really enjoyed my experience directing it, it's something that's been on the horizon for me for quite a long time, but

00:27:41.300 --> 00:27:50.640
directing television is a far different thing from directing a film.  I think you find that television is a producer's medium,

00:27:50.640 --> 00:27:55.460
which is a different thing from film, which is a director's medium.  So, we'd really have to go through an awful lot

00:27:55.460 --> 00:28:00.280
of different people before it came down to me.  I don't know.  Didn't need to ask.

00:28:01.120 --> 00:28:05.140
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: This one is a question-- it's for Emilie, but I don't know this is something you can even answer.

00:28:05.140 --> 00:28:12.460
It's a question about when she was at the well, talking to Rumple.  How in control was Belle?  Or was she doing

00:28:12.460 --> 00:28:15.760
Regina's bidding the entire time?  Can you answer as an actress what you knew?

00:28:15.760 --> 00:28:19.800
&gt;&gt;EMILIE: Yeah.  I love that scene, thanks guys.

00:28:19.800 --> 00:28:20.800
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: It's a great scene.

00:28:20.800 --> 00:28:28.280
&gt;&gt;EMILIE: Um, yeah.  You know, she basically was under Regina's control.

00:28:28.280 --> 00:28:29.080
YVETTE: The entire time?

00:28:29.080 --> 00:28:34.980
&gt;&gt;EMILIE: You know, there's still, from my perspective and how I played it, there's still an element of

00:28:34.980 --> 00:28:42.120
who Belle is as a person there.  Obviously, she's still there and it's not somebody that's completely taken over

00:28:42.120 --> 00:28:50.260
her body in any respect.  But, yeah, you know, still not able to vocalize exactly how she would deal with that

00:28:50.260 --> 00:28:54.140
situation.  Let's put it that way.  So, not terribly in control.

00:28:54.140 --> 00:28:54.900
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Awesome.

00:28:54.900 --> 00:28:55.720
&gt;&gt;EMILIE: But yeah.

00:28:55.720 --> 00:28:56.800
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Sean Maguire.

00:28:56.800 --> 00:28:57.380
&gt;&gt;SEAN: Yes?

00:28:57.380 --> 00:28:58.140
[crowd cheers]

00:28:58.140 --> 00:28:58.840
&gt;&gt;SEAN: Thank you.

00:28:58.840 --> 00:29:04.400
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Um, he's gotten himself into a bit of a pickle.  Hey, I've been a fan of his since "Eve," by the way,

00:29:04.400 --> 00:29:08.300
it was a sitcom he did. Yeah. Y'all know.  UPN.  It's long gone.

00:29:08.300 --> 00:29:15.300
Um, he's in a situation now with Regina and Zelena.  And I found Robin Hood to be a very honorable man.

00:29:15.300 --> 00:29:19.660
So what is the honorable decision in this?  He's got a baby coming, he's in love...

00:29:19.660 --> 00:29:25.440
&gt;&gt;SEAN: Well, I think it is complicated and I think that, you know, when you have a situation like this, the

00:29:25.440 --> 00:29:31.580
best way to deal with it is to go on a show like Maury Povich and just have him figure it out for you.

00:29:31.580 --> 00:29:35.560
Because then you can just sit back and go, "I don't know.  I like them both."

00:29:35.560 --> 00:29:44.020
No, um, I think he's in love with Regina and you know, he-- I got a lot of flack, well Robin Hood got

00:29:44.020 --> 00:29:51.000
a lot of flack for impregnating Zelena.  But he didn't know he was impregnating Zelena.  He thought it was

00:29:51.000 --> 00:29:54.400
his wife.  He was trying to do the right thing.  He was trying to be honorable.  Even though he was

00:29:54.400 --> 00:29:58.920
in love with Regina, he thought "Oh, I'm in this new world, I'll be with my wife, I'll do the right thing."  And then

00:29:58.920 --> 00:30:00.940
turned out, it was her.

00:30:00.940 --> 00:30:02.140
&gt;&gt;REBECCA: Sorry.

00:30:02.140 --> 00:30:06.780
&gt;&gt;SEAN: Uh, so it's caused a lot of problem, but I'm pretty sure Adam and Eddie'll figure a nice

00:30:06.780 --> 00:30:07.820
perfect way...

00:30:07.820 --> 00:30:10.300
&gt;&gt;ADAM: Thanks for spoiling the Maury Povich for me.

00:30:10.300 --> 00:30:11.340
&gt;&gt;SEAN: Sorry!

00:30:11.680 --> 00:30:13.040
I tipped it didn't I?  Sorry.

00:30:13.580 --> 00:30:20.840
But no, I think he's like any decent person, he's trying to do the right thing, but life is messy, and

00:30:20.840 --> 00:30:24.360
complicated, so he'll just have to follow his heart.

00:30:24.360 --> 00:30:29.500
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Alright.  And speaking of following their heart, Regina has to now make some decisions,

00:30:29.500 --> 00:30:34.140
because her sister's back, and her baby's on the way, and it's not her baby, and she can't have babies,

00:30:34.140 --> 00:30:36.660
or can she have babies?  Can she have babies?  Can she reverse it?  Can she have babies?

00:30:36.660 --> 00:30:39.560
I'm looking at you, Adam.  Can she have babies?  Perhaps?  Maybe?

00:30:39.560 --> 00:30:43.320
Okay.  Back to Lana.  I know.  I wanted a little baby Regina.

00:30:43.320 --> 00:30:45.660
&gt;&gt;LANA: We'll see.  Maybe a potion can change that.

00:30:45.660 --> 00:30:51.500
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Yes.  Um, what I loved about the Season 4 Regina is that ultimately, she found out that

00:30:51.500 --> 00:30:56.400
her happiness has to be found within.  It's not a person, it's not a place, it's not a situation,

00:30:56.400 --> 00:31:01.120
it's-- right?  Come on!  It's her realizing that it has to be found within and she's turning around all this

00:31:01.120 --> 00:31:08.380
different programming.  So, in a certain way, Robin was there for some of that, but I think it's more than that

00:31:08.380 --> 00:31:13.000
that made her flip that switch.  In your mind, what was it that made Regina go, "No no no, this is what it is.

00:31:13.000 --> 00:31:14.620
This is what a happy ending is for me."

00:31:14.620 --> 00:31:23.160
&gt;&gt;LANA: I mean, I think it was an evolution and happened over the course of the seasons.  This change, you know,

00:31:23.160 --> 00:31:29.500
I think Emma had a huge influence on her, I think Henry, predominately, had the biggest influence.

00:31:29.500 --> 00:31:38.040
The fear of losing her son is really what prompted her to take a look a herself and start changing.

00:31:40.580 --> 00:31:47.400
Like Regina says, Robin's just a part of her happiness, but he isn't what really--

00:31:47.400 --> 00:31:54.780
I mean he makes her happy, but I think it's that self-growth, and you know, taking a look at oneself and

00:31:54.780 --> 00:32:03.080
really trying to do the right thing and then reaping the benefits of that.  And the outcome for doing the right thing,

00:32:03.080 --> 00:32:12.260
you know, what she receives is love, and friendships, and family, and so it's kind of like a no-brainer.

00:32:12.760 --> 00:32:23.700
So she, yeah.  But it's really because of the family that she's inherited that I think has made a massive influence and change.

00:32:24.020 --> 00:32:28.680
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Speaking of family, Henry... Ugh, Henry.  I know, isn't he great?

00:32:28.680 --> 00:32:29.340
&gt;&gt;LANA: I know.

00:32:29.340 --> 00:32:33.300
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Jared's great.  Okay, um, he snapped the quill.  He became the new Author, and then he

00:32:33.300 --> 00:32:38.760
snapped the quill.  And the Apprentice still said, "We've made the right choice," meaning he was still the Author,

00:32:38.760 --> 00:32:44.160
even though he snapped the quill.  So my question is, is he gonna blog the story now, is it Internet?

00:32:44.160 --> 00:32:44.960
[laughter]

00:32:44.960 --> 00:32:48.320
How are we gonna get our stories without the quill?

00:32:48.320 --> 00:32:50.140
&gt;&gt;ADAM: That's an excellent question.

00:32:50.140 --> 00:32:51.580
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Thank you.

00:32:51.580 --> 00:32:56.740
&gt;&gt;EDDIE: I don't think he thought that through.  You know, Henry was making a heroic gesture, and he

00:32:56.740 --> 00:33:00.200
decided to do the right thing, and I'm sure that won't come back to haunt him.

00:33:00.200 --> 00:33:02.160
&gt;&gt;ADAM: Yeah, he's not gonna regret that at some point.

00:33:02.160 --> 00:33:05.320
&gt;&gt;EDDIE: No, nothing will happen this season that will make him regret that.

00:33:05.320 --> 00:33:06.200
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: No good is coming.

00:33:07.020 --> 00:33:07.820
[laughter]

00:33:08.540 --> 00:33:12.220
&gt;&gt;EDDIE: I think he's gonna text the story.  Or tweet it.

00:33:12.220 --> 00:33:13.120
&gt;&gt;ADAM: A hundred and forty characters.

00:33:13.120 --> 00:33:15.120
&gt;&gt;EDDIE: We're gonna tell it in a hundred and-- how many characters?

00:33:15.120 --> 00:33:16.100
&gt;&gt;ADAM: A hundred forty?

00:33:16.100 --> 00:33:17.040
&gt;&gt;EDDIE: A hundred and forty.

00:33:17.040 --> 00:33:17.780
&gt;&gt;ADAM: I think so.

00:33:17.780 --> 00:33:18.340
&gt;&gt;EDDIE: Yeah.

00:33:18.340 --> 00:33:21.680
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Um, I'm gonna keep asking this question  every year.

00:33:22.220 --> 00:33:27.400
And if you want me to stop asking this question, you either need to do it, or stop adding musical people to the cast.

00:33:28.620 --> 00:33:29.820
Musical episode.

00:33:30.260 --> 00:33:33.120
[crowd cheers]

00:33:35.260 --> 00:33:36.300
Look.  Look, man.

00:33:36.300 --> 00:33:37.340
&gt;&gt;EDDIE: I mean.

00:33:37.340 --> 00:33:39.900
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Look at these people.  They want it!

00:33:39.900 --> 00:33:40.500
[crowd cheers]

00:33:40.500 --> 00:33:46.160
You got Sean, you got Colin, you got Josh, there's so many musical people--

00:33:46.160 --> 00:33:47.160
&gt;&gt;EDDIE: We really do.

00:33:47.160 --> 00:33:50.520
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Their voices, all the accents they do-- You know they can sing, everybody up here can sing.  Come on now.

00:33:50.520 --> 00:33:51.820
&gt;&gt;EDDIE: You guys wanna sing someday?

00:33:51.820 --> 00:33:52.780
&gt;&gt;CAST: Yeah!

00:33:52.780 --> 00:33:54.860
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: They want to do this!

00:33:54.860 --> 00:34:01.860
&gt;&gt;EDDIE: Well, you know what, it would be great to do a musical episode, I don't know really even where to begin.

00:34:02.020 --> 00:34:03.860
Does anyone have any songs?

00:34:04.200 --> 00:34:06.040
&gt;&gt;ADAM: Are there any songwriters out there?

00:34:06.040 --> 00:34:09.080
&gt;&gt;EDDIE: Any "Once Upon A Time" songwriters out there?

00:34:09.140 --> 00:34:15.700
"It's Beginning to Look A Lot Like a Dark Curse is Coming" would be, I think, what we would open with.

00:34:15.700 --> 00:34:18.740
And then, go, "It's a Good Time For Granny's."

00:34:18.740 --> 00:34:20.820
&gt;&gt;JENNIFER: "Purple Smoke."  "Purple Smoke" would be a good title.

00:34:20.820 --> 00:34:26.080
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Uh, I have a quick Camelot question.  Does this exist in the same time that

00:34:26.080 --> 00:34:28.020
Killian was in the Royal Army-- Navy?

00:34:28.020 --> 00:34:30.900
Navy?  Is it possible that our Hook-- Colin?

00:34:30.900 --> 00:34:37.860
&gt;&gt;EDDIE: Camelot's going to exist in a-- Adam why don't you answer that because I don't know how to say it.

00:34:37.860 --> 00:34:42.140
&gt;&gt;ADAM: Camelot exists in a parallel timeline--

00:34:42.140 --> 00:34:42.640
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Parallel timeline.

00:34:42.640 --> 00:34:49.460
&gt;&gt;ADAM: with everything.  So it's existed, and how we portray it in the show, you'll see that's existed long ago,

00:34:49.460 --> 00:34:51.100
short ago, present ago,

00:34:51.100 --> 00:34:51.680
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Short ago.

00:34:51.680 --> 00:34:53.840
&gt;&gt;ADAM: and maybe in the future.

00:34:53.840 --> 00:34:54.340
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Okay.

00:34:54.340 --> 00:34:57.680
&gt;&gt;ADAM: But, uh, yes, it may have coexisted with that time period.

00:34:57.680 --> 00:35:01.180
&gt;&gt;YVETTE; Okay.  And, um, this is another question I got on Twitter from a lot of people.

00:35:01.180 --> 00:35:03.980
Is there an illustrator of the story book?

00:35:03.980 --> 00:35:04.860
&gt;&gt;CAST: Ooh.

00:35:04.860 --> 00:35:05.780
&gt;&gt;ADAM : An illustrator.

00:35:05.780 --> 00:35:08.880
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: You guys, look, there's pictures.  It's not just words, it's pictures, too.

00:35:08.880 --> 00:35:09.680
&gt;&gt;JENNIFER: An illustrator.

00:35:09.680 --> 00:35:10.440
&gt;&gt;LANA: I love that question.

00:35:10.440 --> 00:35:12.700
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Isaac didn't look like he was an artist.

00:35:12.700 --> 00:35:15.180
&gt;&gt;EDDIE: This year, the search for the sketch artist is on!

00:35:16.640 --> 00:35:18.420
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Send your résumés.

00:35:18.420 --> 00:35:20.680
&gt;&gt;EDDIE: It's a good question.  We gotta look into the illustrator.

00:35:21.520 --> 00:35:26.360
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: I wanna ask this question for Ginny and Josh.  This is a quick one, we're gonna do this quick.

00:35:26.360 --> 00:35:30.460
How has being parents in real life changed how you're parents on "Once Upon A Time"? Go.

00:35:31.420 --> 00:35:32.860
&gt;&gt;JOSH: How has what?

00:35:32.860 --> 00:35:37.540
&gt;&gt;GINNIFER: How is being parents changing your life as Charming?

00:35:37.540 --> 00:35:38.580
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: You didn't hear me, Josh?

00:35:38.580 --> 00:35:39.380
[laughter]

00:35:39.380 --> 00:35:40.460
&gt;&gt;JENNIFER: They're so tired they don't understand the question.

00:35:40.460 --> 00:35:40.960
&gt;&gt;GINNIFER: We're just--

00:35:40.960 --> 00:35:42.680
&gt;&gt;JOSH: I do it with lots of sleep.  A lot of sleep.

00:35:42.680 --> 00:35:48.520
No, it changes everything.  It changes how you think about everything.  Literally everything.

00:35:48.520 --> 00:35:50.120
The world, what you do--

00:35:50.120 --> 00:35:53.240
&gt;&gt;GINNIFER: To see your heart beat outside your body, it changes the stakes, I feel.

00:35:53.240 --> 00:35:59.180
I mean, I don't have to imagine anything now.  Any threat to Emma and I have a full-blown panic attack,

00:35:59.180 --> 00:36:01.660
just as I would for poor Oliver there.

00:36:01.660 --> 00:36:05.300
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: There's a couple of housekeeping things I wanna do first.  First off, I wanna tell you that those of you

00:36:05.300 --> 00:36:11.840
in Florida-- in Lake Buena Vista, Florida, Mr. Gold's Pawnbroker and Antiquities Dealer storefront display is

00:36:11.840 --> 00:36:12.980
open at Disney's Hollywood Studios.

00:36:12.980 --> 00:36:17.920
That's the first thing.  Second,  we did not get a lot of questions in from the audience and I'm sorry, but

00:36:17.920 --> 00:36:22.200
there was a reason I didn't pick a lot.  And the reason is this: The next ten people that were in line are getting

00:36:22.200 --> 00:36:27.840
tickets to the signing.  So I didn't call you because I wanted you to get to meet them.  Now you love me.  Now you love me.

00:36:27.840 --> 00:36:28.760
[laughter]

00:36:28.760 --> 00:36:31.480
And you guys wanted to say one more thing?

00:36:31.480 --> 00:36:37.660
&gt;&gt;ADAM: Yeah, there's one more thing we wanna show you.  So, if you just hang around...

00:36:37.660 --> 00:36:43.240
It's a little bit of a surprise we hope, and we hope you enjoy it.  It's a little peek at something we're gonna be

00:36:43.240 --> 00:36:46.880
doing in Season 5.  And thank you all for coming, and thank you all for watching.

00:36:46.880 --> 00:36:48.500
&gt;&gt;YVETTE: Thanks for coming, you guys!

00:36:48.500 --> 00:36:49.780
&gt;&gt;CAST: Thank you!

